BH may already be partly covered by BIG-bench, and MATH Level 5 is not queried because the gap memo does not list it as a search topic. The retrieval step can resolve the individual papers.\n\n## Exclusions\nThe gap memo deliberately does not flag the rank-Gauss transform, kNN, numeric results, protocol facts, or the limitations and discussion text. No queries are planned for these. Queries must not name or hint at the prior published paper on this exact task.\n  232 references.bib\n  188 postdraft_references.bib\n  420 total\n3a4\n> @inproceedings{Zheng2023MTBench,\n7a9\n> @article{Zhuo2024BigCodeBench,\n21a24\n> @inproceedings{Krause2007ObservationSelection,\n24,30c27\n< @article{Hofmann2025Fluid,\n< @article{Zhou2023IFEval,\n< @inproceedings{Suzgun2023BBH,\n< @article{Rein2023GPQA,\n< @article{Sprague2023MuSR,\n< @inproceedings{Wang2024MMLUPro,\n< @article{Hendrycks2021MATH,\n---\n> @inproceedings{Vania2021ComparingTestSets,\n[semantic_scholar] search start | query 4/6 | redundancy and correlation among LLM benchmarks low-dimensional structure of benchmark scores\n[semantic_scholar] search failed | query 4/6 | redundancy and correlation among LLM benchmarks low-dimensional structure of benchmark scores | Semantic Scholar HTTP 429 for https://api.semanticscholar.org/graph/v1/paper/search?query=redundancy+and+correlation+among+LLM+benchmarks+low-dimensional+structure+of+benchmark+scores&limit=25&fields=paperId%2Ctitle%2Cyear%2Cvenue%2CcitationCount\n[semantic_scholar] search start | query 5/6 | Open LLM Leaderboard v2 evaluation of open language models\n[semantic_scholar] search complete | [####--------] | refs 9/25 (16 left) | candidates 0/25 | query 5/6\n[semantic_scholar] fetching | [#####-------] | refs 10/25 (15 left) | candidates 1/25 | query 5/6\n[semantic_scholar] fetching | [#####-------] | refs 11/25 (14 left) | candidates 2/25 | query 5/6\n[semantic_scholar] fetching | [######------] | refs 12/25 (13 left) | candidates 3/25 | query 5/6\n[semantic_scholar