{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B7hs4oKDGaYFBhMgDX2Bty","type":"tool_result","content":"paper.tex:192:Because several components change together and the two seeds share one held-out set, this licenses only the statement that the richer configuration was better on that partition; it does not attribute the gain to the transform, the wrapper selector or the stack. The pair extended with a latent-skill member and a latent A-optimal selector produced the same four metrics as the proposed pair to all reported digits. The extension is kept only if it improves cross-validation error, which is consistent with it being inactive, but no diagnostic recording the choice was retained, so the cause is unknown, and we treat this configuration as a null result. The sealed evaluation was run on one of these two configurations; the exact tie means the retained scores cannot say which (Supplementary Information).\npaper.tex:295:Entry point: a single Python file exposing a \\texttt{handle} request function (operations \\texttt{reset}, \\texttt{load\\_history}, \\texttt{select}, \\texttt{predict}); dependencies are NumPy only; behaviour is deterministic given the seed except for the wall-clock guards. Figures and tables in this paper come from \\texttt{scripts/build\\_figures.py} (Figure~\\ref{fig:main}), \\texttt{scripts/extract\\_protocol\\_facts.py} (Table~\\ref{tab:data}), \\texttt{scripts/extract\\_search\\_metrics.py} (Tables~\\ref{tab:search} and~\\ref{tab:seeds}); the sealed metrics are read from the evaluation registry. The data come from the public upstream sources and pinned revisions listed in Table~\\ref{tab:data}; licence terms of these sources were not verified in this study. Literature retrieval used only titles from the starter literature and standard methodology references; no material from the excluded publication was knowingly accessed.\n.claude/skills/validate-paper/:\nSKILL.md\nscripts\ntemplates\n\n.claude/skills/validate-